{
 "encounter_id": "00957",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR",
  "person_3": "NURSE"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_3",
   "t": "Morning, Dr Pritchard. I've done Mr Ashworth's obs: blood pressure 128 over 82, pulse 74, weight 92 kilos. He's a bit worried about his liver test."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you, nurse. Come in, Mr Ashworth. I understand there's an abnormal liver test from your insurance check?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes. They sent a letter. The, er, the thing, the numbers, were high. I can't remember which. The liver ones, anyway. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's what we'll look at. Tell me, any symptoms at the moment? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I get tired, but I'm fifty-eight, and I work too much."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any pain, anywhere in the tummy?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "A dull ache on the right side, under the ribs, mostly after a fatty meal. I had a fish and chip supper last week and it was there all night."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any bloating?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, a bit, after big meals."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any yellowing of the skin or eyes?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. My wife would've said."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "What medicines do you take?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "One tablet for cholesterol. A little blue one. I couldn't tell you the name, I'm sorry. My wife usually knows."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "We'll find it on your record. How's your general health?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "High cholesterol, as I said, and I'm overweight, I know."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me press on your tummy. Take a deep breath in.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Okay. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "There's no tenderness over the liver, and I can't feel it enlarged."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's good? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Any problem with your bowels, anything different?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No, nothing, they're normal."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Here's what I think. Mild liver test abnormalities with high cholesterol and extra weight is most often a fatty liver. That's my provisional thinking."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fatty liver. From drink? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Not necessarily. It's more often from weight, sugar and fat in the diet. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I don't drink much. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. The main treatment is gradual weight loss, about five to ten percent of your weight, and cutting down on fatty and sugary foods."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "That's about nine kilos. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Roughly. Slowly, over the next six months. Walk for half an hour every day."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll do it. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And I'd like you to bring the box for the cholesterol tablet next time, so we can note the name properly. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll ask my wife. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to see you again in six weeks."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Six weeks. Thank you. ~"
  }
 ],
